# ClaimPilot AI environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` in the project root and edit. `.env` is git-ignored — never
# commit real credentials. All values below are placeholders only.
#
# Required:
#   DATABASE_URL  SQLAlchemy URL and the single source of truth for the
#                 database target (application code never overrides it).
#                   Local development / tests — no external service needed:
#                     DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./claimpilot.db
#                   PostgreSQL (e.g. Supabase) — the URL scheme token selects
#                   the driver; both ship in requirements.txt:
#                     DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:password@localhost:5432/claimpilot
#                     DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:password@localhost:5432/claimpilot
#                   A bare postgresql:// URL selects psycopg (v3) on
#                   SQLAlchemy 2.1+ (psycopg2 on 2.0).
#                 Required in APP_ENV=production: a missing value fails fast
#                 rather than silently falling back. Outside production a
#                 missing value falls back to the local SQLite file above
#                 (with a warning). PostgreSQL connections use a bounded
#                 connect timeout (see POSTGRES_CONNECT_TIMEOUT).
#   PYTHONPATH    Must be `src` so the backend and tests can import `claimpilot`.
#
# Schema management:
#   Production schema is owned by Alembic. Run `alembic upgrade head` as a
#   deploy step; the app never runs create_all in production. Outside
#   production create_all runs at startup so a fresh checkout just works.
#
# Optional:
#   APP_ENV        Environment label (development / production), default: development
#   LOG_LEVEL      Logging verbosity, default: INFO
#   API_AUTH_TOKEN Shared bearer token that gates the sensitive API routers
#                  (claims, analyses, reviews, dashboard). Not an individual
#                  reviewer identity — it authenticates the client only.
#                    - Set:    every protected request must send
#                              `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (401 if missing,
#                              403 if wrong).
#                    - Unset:  the API runs WITHOUT authentication outside
#                              production (a warning is logged). In
#                              APP_ENV=production a missing token is a fatal
#                              misconfiguration: readiness reports not-ready.
#                  Never commit the real value; use a long random string.
#   CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS
#                  Comma-separated browser origins allowed by CORS, e.g.
#                  `http://localhost:5173,https://claims.example.com`.
#                  Explicit origins only; the wildcard `*` is rejected.
#                  Empty (default) means no CORS headers are added, which
#                  preserves same-origin and the Vite dev proxy.
#   Model/data artifact paths (all optional; relative paths resolve from the
#   project root, absolute paths are used as-is so a deployment can mount an
#   artifact store):
#     FRAUD_MODEL_PATH       default models/fraud_model_v1.joblib
#     SEVERITY_MODEL_PATH    default models/severity_model_v1.joblib
#     ANOMALY_MODEL_PATH     default models/anomaly_model_v1.joblib
#     RISK_CONFIG_PATH       default configs/risk_scoring.json
#     DECISION_POLICY_PATH   default configs/decision_policy.json
#     DATA_PROCESSED_PATH    default data/processed/processed_all.csv
#   The model binaries and the processed dataset are NOT committed to Git; a
#   fresh checkout must obtain them (see README "Model and data artifacts").
#   A missing artifact fails fast at startup with an actionable message.
#
# Local verification (tests, manual checks) should use SQLite. Point
# DATABASE_URL at PostgreSQL only when you intend to use that database.

DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:password@localhost:5432/claimpilot
APP_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
PYTHONPATH=src
# API_AUTH_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-secret
# CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
